  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;be three real numbers such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>y</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>z</mi></mfrac></math> are in an arithmetic progression and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></math> are in a geometric progression. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>z</mi></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is equal to"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "150",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>y</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>z</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;are in AP and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi></math>&nbsp;are in GP.</p><p>As given, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>y</mi></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math><br />Also,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Also given that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>z</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>y</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>z</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>iii</mi></mfenced></math><br />From <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></math> we get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>iv</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Now from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">v</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Now using <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>Hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn></math></p><p>Therefore, this is the required answer.</p></blockquote>"
